# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before it reads a single
# instruction, so anything listed here is a cost paid on every build of every
# image whether or not a Dockerfile would have used it. Without this file the
# context was 20GB — build artefacts and git worktrees, none of which any image
# copies — and sending it took longer than compiling.
#
# Each entry is something that is either rebuilt inside the image or has no
# business in one.

# Rust build artefacts. The images compile from source; a host target directory
# is both useless to them and the single largest thing in the tree.
api/target/
sdk/rust/target/

# Installed and generated by the web image itself.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
sdk/typescript/node_modules/
sdk/typescript/dist/
sdk/typescript/coverage/

# Agent worktrees and tool state. Each worktree is a full checkout with its own
# build artefacts, so a handful of them outweighs the repository many times over.
.claude/
.gstack/

# History, not source. Nothing in any image reads it.
.git/
.github/*
!.github/scripts/
.github/scripts/*
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-loopback.patch
!.github/scripts/bubblewrap-loopback-test.c

# Editor and platform leavings.
.DS_Store
*.swp
